"## Summary\n\nUpdater follow-up 25: F30-01's `update-good` exit 3, under D-158 as revised.\n- **Session:** launched 01:58 EST on 2026-11-04 on #458's roadmap row. It stopped with a diagnosis at 02:12, was resumed at 02:23 on the revised D-158, and delivered at 03:00.\n- **Model:** codex `gpt-6-astra`.\n- **Size:** 8 commits and 9 owned files, +1,141/−6.\n  - The production change is about 90 lines in `node/updater`: the new `lock_wait.go`, plus `engine.go` and one line each in `pending.go`, `result.go` and `seed.go`.\n  - The rest is two proof files, the updater guide and the dated note.\n- **Checks:**\n  - merge-tree clean on current `main`; prepush-scan clean; owned-check passes.\n  - **The orchestrator reran these** on a scratch tree: current `main` (after #461) with netlab 35 and this branch merged in. All pass:\n    - `go test ./node/updater/... ./node/nodelock/...`, including the real default-budget proofs;\n    - the D-158, follow-up 24 and r29 proofs by name, 12 top-level tests, all passing;\n    - the consumers: `go test ./node/agent/... ./packaging/installer/... ./tests/e2e/at/updates/...`, and the live-tagged update ATs compiled with `-run '^$'`;\n    - `go test ./tests/handover/...`;\n    - `go vet ./node/... ./packaging/...` and `make go-lint`;\n    - `fvpn-updater` built for linux amd64 and arm64;\n    - gofmt and `git diff --check`.\n- **Scope:** no lab, live acceptance, reservation or Docker object. The common lock library, the exit table and D-034g are unchanged.\n\n**The orchestrator's reading.**\n- **The diagnosis came first, and the lane's stop was right.**\n  - The agent's ordinary hold of `update.lock` is bounded by its Step's local deadline, about 10 s (`node/agent/engine.go:680–684`, `serving.go:246–251`), not by the sampled half-second. So the brief's 2 s bound was not supported by the code.\n  - `seed`, `apply` and standalone `flush` can overlap a serving agent, as `run` does.\n  - Today's stale details already retried for the nominal 80 ms, not \"at once\".\n  - The orchestrator revised D-158 on these findings, and the lane resumed.\n- **The change, under the revised D-158.**\n  - **Four commands wait.** `run`, `seed`, `apply` and standalone `flush` wait for a live holder within one 10 s budget, `updateLockWaitBudget`, polling every 20 ms.\n  - **Past the budget:** exit 3, with the unchanged line `fvpn-updater: updater: UPDATE_BUSY: lock`.\n  - **Unchanged:**\n    - `recover` and a standalone `Retain` keep five attempts 20 ms apart;\n    - nested callers reuse the outer holder and never wait;\n    - stale details keep exit 1 after five attempts, counted from the first stale answer;\n    - unreadable metadata stays a live holder.\n  - **Cancellation** ends the wait at once.\n  - **The record:** one JSON slog record, `msg=\"update lock wait\"`, with `command`, `waited_ms`, `acquired` and `budget_ms`. It is written only after a missed first attempt, so an uncontended command's stderr is unchanged.\n- **Proofs, with a real second holder of the lock file.**\n  - **A 600 ms holder,** for all four commands: exit 3 at about 81 ms before the change, and exit 0 at about 617 ms after it.\n  - **The CLI's real default budget:** exit 3 at 10.006 s, never early, with the exact error line and every record field.\n  - **The rest:**\n    - every stale detail on every command still exits 1 at about 81 ms;\n    - a live-to-stale transition returns 86 ms after the first stale answer;\n    - `recover` and `Retain` behave as before;\n    - cancellation ends at about 300 ms.\n  - **Existing tests:** r29's four proofs and follow-up 24's five tests pass unchanged. No existing assertion pinned an 80 ms window for a budgeted command.\n  - **Consumers:** the installer's seed capture, the agent's recovery child and the update ATs pass unchanged. They read the exit status, not the stderr's shape.\n- **The orchestrator's code review.**\n  - **`withLockFor` checks `lockHeld` before choosing a path,** so seal's `Flush`, `Run`'s inner `Recover` and a nested `Retain` take no wait.\n  - **Each poll is one call to the unchanged `nodelock.AcquireWithBootID`.** The last sleep is clipped to the remaining budget, which matches the 10.006 s proof.\n  - **Once a stale answer appears,** the five-attempt window is not clipped by the budget. So a live-then-stale sequence near the budget can end up to about 80 ms past it. That matches \"counted from the first stale answer\".\n  - **A non-busy first-attempt error,** such as a permission error, also writes the record, with `acquired=false`, before the unchanged error line. That fits the revision's \"the first attempt does not get the lock\". Noted, not a defect.\n- **F30-01 stays open** until an acceptance run reaches the real candidate and passes.\n- **Next:**\n  - **Devstack 35 is armed on this merge.** It retains each updater invocation's output, which `deploy/devstack/entrypoint-node.sh` now overwrites, and runs the candidate path.\n  - **The operator sentence** goes to handover's next follow-up.\n"
